.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH fleetring-context-add 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-context\-add \- Adds a context: a name for a fleet\*(Aqs control addresses and identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring context add\fR [\fB\-\-fleet\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-ca\fR] [\fB\-\-cert\fR] [\fB\-\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-control\fR> <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds a context: a name for a fleet\*(Aqs control addresses and identity
.PP
The identity is its certificates and principal. The first context added becomes current.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-control\fR \fI<CONTROL>\fR
A control node\*(Aqs address, `host:port`

Repeat it for more; they are tried in order.
.TP
\fB\-\-fleet\fR \fI<FLEET>\fR
The fleet\*(Aqs name

Defaults to the fleet the client certificate names.
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-dir\fR \fI<TLS_DIR>\fR
A directory with `ca.crt` and the client certificates `cert client` writes
.TP
\fB\-\-ca\fR \fI<CA>\fR
The trusted authority certificate, PEM
.TP
\fB\-\-cert\fR \fI<CERT>\fR
The client certificate, PEM
.TP
\fB\-\-key\fR \fI<KEY>\fR
The client certificate\*(Aqs private key, PEM
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<PRINCIPAL>\fR
The principal to act as

With `\-\-tls\-dir`, `client.<principal>.crt` is the certificate.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\-file\fR \fI<TOKEN_FILE>\fR
A file that holds a bearer token

The context stores the path, never the token.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
The new context\*(Aqs name

1 to 63 lowercase letters, digits, \*(Aq\-\*(Aq, \*(Aq_\*(Aq or \*(Aq.\*(Aq.
